  "description": "Drive a real browser with the agent-browser CLI (headless Chromium over CDP). Use for any browser task: verifying a UI change, taking a screenshot, walking a web page, filling a form, extracting page text, reproducing a frontend bug, or attaching UI evidence to a PR, issue, Linear comment, or Slack thread. Starts with a `command -v agent-browser` check and falls back to manual QA on the slim worker image. Screenshots are kept on agent-fs and embedded in GitHub as user attachments. This is the only browser automation tool; do not use qa-use.",
